Preamble

The GNU General Public License is a free, copyleft license
for software and other kinds of works.

This version of the GPL is designed to ensure your freedom to
share and change all versions of a program--to make sure it
does what you want it to do and to protect the community's
decision to keep it free.

When we speak of free software, we are referring to freedom,
not price. Our General Public Licenses are designed to make sure
that you have the freedom to distribute copies of free software
(and charge for this service if you wish), that you receive
source code or can get it if you want it, that you can change
the software and share your changes with others, and that you
are informed about your rights. We protect your rights with
four essential freedoms:

 0. To run the program as you wish, for any purpose (freedom 0).

 1. To study and change the program (freedom 1). Access to the
    source code is a precondition for this.

 2. To redistribute copies of the original program (freedom 2).

 3. To distribute copies of your modified versions to others.
    By doing this you can give the whole community a chance to
    benefit from your changes. Access to the source code is a
    precondition for this.

This is how freedom is protected in our license.

You may not use the software to restrict the rights of others.

 0. This License applies to any program or other work which
    contains a notice placed by the copyright holder saying it
    is governed by this License.

       Each licensee is addressed as "you".

You accept the license if you copy, modify or distribute the
work.  Therefore, you need to keep it intact so that everyone
else also receives it. You may not impose any further
restrictions on the exercise of the rights granted herein.

 1. You may not use the software to restrict the core
    freedoms of others. This includes but is not limited to
    the act of using the software to promote dependency on a
    service or software that is unavailable on the same terms as
the original program.

 2. To protect your rights, we need to restrict some of your
    actions. For example, the work may not be broken down into
    multiple parts in a way that allows you to make parts
    proprietary, or to disallow use of the work on
    remote servers.

General Terms

 0. You may copy and distribute verbatim copies of this
    License document, but changing it is not allowed.

 1. You may change the program and charge for it, but if you do
    you must provide those you give the program to with the same
    freedoms you received.  That means they also should have
